  "stem": "In the \\(xy\\)-plane, a line passes through the points \\((-2, -5)\\) and \\((4, 4)\\). The point \\((k, 2k)\\) lies on this line, where \\(k\\) is a constant. What is the value of \\(k\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "-4"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Slope \\(= \\frac{4 - (-5)}{4 - (-2)} = \\frac{3}{2}\\). Through \\((4, 4)\\): \\(y = \\frac{3}{2}x - 2\\).",
    "Substitute \\((k, 2k)\\): \\(2k = \\frac{3}{2}k - 2\\), so \\(\\frac{1}{2}k = -2\\) and \\(k = -4\\)."
  ],
  "verify": "x, k = symbols('x k')\nm = Rational(4 - (-5), 4 - (-2))\nline = m*(x - 4) + 4\nsol = solve(Eq(2*k, line.subs(x, k)), k)\nassert sol == [-4]\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == sol",
